# field_seq_bound.sby — FIELD.SEQ.CORE's anti-hang law.
#
# The law is stated in design/contracts/FIELD.SEQ.CORE.md and again beside the
# port itself: `instr_count_i` is a LIVENESS bound, not a semantic check. The
# decoder validates programs; this block does not re-check them. But the
# instruction MEMORY belongs to the shell, and a walk with no bound turns a
# mis-loaded memory into a machine that hangs forever instead of one that
# reports ST_PC_OVERRUN.
#
# THAT IS NOT SOMETHING THE DIFFERENTIAL CAN PROVE. tests/differential/
# field_seq_directed.cpp runs 906 directed and 2,506 random programs, and every
# one of them is a program somebody chose. A hang is what happens on the
# program nobody chose. Here `ins_op_i` and every operand field are FREE, so
# the solver may feed the sequencer opcodes that do not exist and operands
# pointing anywhere, changing them every cycle — which is exactly what a
# mis-loaded memory is.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required (ledger rule V16):
#   bmc    — a_pc_bounded, a_op_bounded and a_progress hold to the depth below.
#   cover  — the antecedents are REACHABLE. Both properties are implications
#            over a busy machine, and a model that never starts satisfies them
#            while proving nothing. That is the shape MEM.GUARD's lane failed
#            in and DEBUG.FRAMEBLIT's nearly did; the covers here demand that
#            the machine RUNS, that it finishes cleanly, that it OVERRUNS, and
#            that it refuses an unsupported opcode.
#
# THE DEPTH IS DERIVED FROM THE PROPERTIES, 2026-08-23 -- AND IT IS 172, NOT 180.
#
# 180 was a round number, which is the proof-side version of carrying a 72-bit
# operand because slack looks free. The question a depth has to answer is: what
# is the SHORTEST window in which each assertion can actually be VIOLATED?
# Shallower and the assertion is decoration; deeper and the extra steps buy
# nothing while costing solver time superlinearly.
#
# `zhao_field_seq_pkg` declares MAX_OP_CYCLES = 80 -- the ceiling on ONE
# instruction, measured at 67 for the worst of them (NORMALIZE3) by section 12
# of tests/differential/field_seq_directed.cpp. The harness imports it and
# derives everything else:
#
#     FORMAL_PROLOGUE  = 2                                   (see below)
#     MAX_RUN_CYCLES   = 2 * MAX_OP_CYCLES + 8       = 168
#     PROVEN_DEPTH     = FORMAL_PROLOGUE + MAX_RUN_CYCLES + 2 = 172
#
# THE PROLOGUE IS TWO CYCLES AND BOTH ARE FORCED BY THE HARNESS. Step 0 has
# `f_past_valid == 0`, which assumes `!rst_n`: nothing is asserted and the
# machine is held in reset. Step 1 is the earliest `rst_n` may rise, and the
# sequencer sits in Q_IDLE waiting for `start_i`. So the walk cannot be busy
# before step 2.
#
# WHICH ASSERTION BINDS, and it is not the obvious one:
#
#   a_op_bounded  needs the LAST of two instructions to be able to reach
#                 MAX_OP_CYCLES + 1. The worst ordering is instruction one
#                 taking its full allowance and instruction two overrunning:
#                 2 + 80 + 81 = 163.
#   a_progress    needs `busy_cnt` to be able to reach MAX_RUN_CYCLES + 1:
#                 2 + 169 = 171. THIS IS THE BINDING ONE, and it is not
#                 redundant with the first -- a machine could retire every
#                 instruction inside 80 clocks and still never leave `busy`,
#                 and only this counter would see that.
#
# 171 plus one cycle to reach Q_DONE and one of slack is 172.
#
# V19: `a_scope_short_program_window` is pinned to PROVEN_DEPTH, so raising the
# depth past the window it was derived for FIRES rather than silently re-scoping
# what PASS means. The reduced window asserts itself.
#
# It used to be a bare `busy_cnt <= 120` at depth 140, with a paragraph
# explaining why 120 was generous. The DSP rearchitecture of 2026-08-23 made the
# ops longer -- every one now waits on a shared multiplier, a shared root and a
# shared reciprocal -- so a number chosen against the old schedule would have had
# to be EDITED, which is how a bound stops being one.
#
# Frontend: read_slang reading the REAL frozen zhao_pkg.sv and the REAL
# generated zhao_abi_pkg.sv, and the real unit blocks the sequencer
# instantiates — no stubs. --unroll-limit is raised for zhao_crc32c_fold's
# sibling reason: several of these blocks derive constants at elaboration.
#
# Run via `ctest -L formal` (test formal_field_seq_bound) or by hand with
# cwd = tests/formal:
#   sby -f --prefix <workdir> field_seq_bound.sby

[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 172
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 172
expect pass

[engines]
btor btormc

[script]
read_slang --unroll-limit=200000 --top zhao_field_seq_bound_harness -DFORMAL zhao_abi_pkg.sv zhao_pkg.sv zhao_field_rcp_rom.sv zhao_field_rcp24_rom.sv zhao_field_sin_rom.sv zhao_field_mul.sv zhao_field_exec_shared.sv zhao_field_alu.sv zhao_field_rcp.sv zhao_field_sin.sv zhao_field_isqrt.sv zhao_field_len.sv zhao_field_normalize.sv zhao_field_curve.sv zhao_field_noise.sv zhao_field_ring.sv zhao_field_rot.sv zhao_field_seq.sv field_seq_bound_harness.sv
prep -top zhao_field_seq_bound_harness

# =============================================================================
# THE bmc TASK RUNS ON AN ABSTRACTED MODEL. THE cover TASK DOES NOT.
# =============================================================================
# READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING THIS LANE AS EVIDENCE. An abstracted proof that does
# not announce itself reads as stronger than it is, which is worse than no proof
# at all. `design/formal_runs.yml` says the same thing in its notes, so a
# reviewer deciding whether a maturity claim is backed sees it there too.
#
# WHAT IS ABSTRACTED. `cutpoint` replaces the shared multiplier's product wire
# with a value the solver may choose freely every cycle, and `opt_clean` then
# deletes the multiplier that no longer drives anything. BOTH PASSES ARE
# REQUIRED: without the opt_clean the dead multiplier stays in the netlist and
# nothing is saved. Verified rather than assumed — the model goes from 4 `$mul`
# cells to 1, and the survivor is a multiply by a constant.
#
# WHY. The 2026-08-23 rearchitecture put a registered signed 33x33 multiplier in
# this cone, and a bounded model checker must reason about every bit of it at
# every unrolled step. Unabstracted, this proof took two hours and twenty
# minutes to reach k = 114 of 180 and was still slowing down. That is a lane CI
# will not run, and a lane nobody runs is decoration — this project has already
# been bitten once by a gate that skipped itself and hid weeks of drift.
#
# WHY THE DIRECTION IS SOUND. A free product is an OVER-APPROXIMATION: the
# abstract machine does everything the real one does and more. For a SAFETY
# property — `pc <= instr_count_i`, `op_cnt <= MAX_OP_CYCLES`, `busy_cnt <=
# MAX_RUN_CYCLES` — a proof over the superset proves it over the design. The
# abstraction can produce a SPURIOUS COUNTEREXAMPLE; it cannot produce a
# spurious PASS. That is the correct direction here.
#
# WHY IT IS ALSO NON-LOSSY, WHICH IS THE PART THAT MATTERS. The bound is
# STRUCTURAL: every operation walks a FIXED schedule, so its cycle count does
# not depend on any product's value. RCP is three issues; the integer root is
# thirty-four iterations whatever the operand; CURVE's binary search is six
# steps counted by `k`, and the comparison inside it moves `lo`, not the state;
# RING walks nine products and two reciprocal calls; NOISE branches on the
# opcode and on a lane counter; ROT and LEN are straight-line. Audited, one FSM
# at a time, by reading every `state <=` in the cone.
#
# THERE IS EXACTLY ONE EXCEPTION AND IT IS WORTH NAMING. `zhao_field_normalize`
# branches on `is_zero`, which is `n2 == 0` — and `n2` IS a sum of products. So
# one transition in the engine does depend on a product value. It is harmless
# here for a reason that has to be checked rather than hoped: BOTH branches are
# fixed-length, and the zero branch is the SHORT one (straight to N_OUT) while
# the non-zero branch is the long one (the reciprocal walk). The abstract
# machine may take either, so it may always take the LONGER — which is exactly
# the case the bound has to cover. The abstraction therefore cannot hide a
# violation; it can only offer the solver the worst case more freely.
#
# WHAT WOULD MAKE THIS UNSOUND — or rather, sound but useless. If any operation
# terminated on a DATA-DEPENDENT condition — a convergence test, an early-out on
# a comparison against a product, a normalise loop that iterates until a bit is
# set — then a free product could spin it forever and the proof would fail with
# a counterexample that cannot happen. Passing would then be luck. No operation
# in this engine is written that way, and if one ever is, this comment is the
# place that stops being true.
#
# THE cover TASK IS DELIBERATELY NOT ABSTRACTED. Its whole job is to show the
# antecedents are reachable in the REAL design; reaching them with a product the
# multiplier could never produce would prove nothing, and would be precisely the
# vacuity the covers exist to rule out. The `bmc:` prefixes below are what keep
# the two apart.
bmc: cutpoint w:u_seq.u_exec.u_mul.p_o
bmc: opt_clean -purge

